.TH WELLUTILS 1 "September 2026" "wellutils 1.4.0-55" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
wellutils \- launcher and suite of system/peripheral reporting tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellutils
[\fB\-\-lang\fR \fIru|en\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR|\fIalias\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellutils
is the entry point of a suite of shell tools that render system reports with
adaptive box-drawing, colour and emoji. It dispatches to the individual tools
and can set the persistent report language.
.PP
When invoked without arguments, it prints the suite help.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS AND ALIASES
.TP
.B wellper, per, wper
Peripheral report (USB, displays, audio).
.TP
.B wellhw, hw, whw
Hardware summary (CPU, GPU, board, RAM, storage, cooling).
.TP
.B wellmem, mem, wmem
Memory detail.
.TP
.B wellsensors, sensors, wsensors, wtemp
Temperature and sensor monitor (CPU, GPU, disks via smartctl/nvme).
.TP
.B wellusb, usb, wusb
USB device listing with ID database lookup.
.TP
.B wellpci, pci, wpci
PCI device listing grouped by class.
.TP
.B wellblock, block, wblock
Block devices with partitions and mount points.
.TP
.B wellmod, mod, wmod
Loaded kernel modules, top-10 and grouped by category.
.TP
.B wellfetch, fetch, wfetch
System information display with an ANSI logo.
.TP
.B wellcpu, cpu, wcpu
CPU detail: model, sockets, cores, threads, caches, load.
.TP
.B wellgpu, gpu, wgpu
GPU detail with live nvidia-smi stats when available.
.TP
.B wellup, up, wup
Cross-distro system updater; \fB\-\-self-update\fR also updates the suite itself.
.TP
.B wellnet, net, wnet
Offline network overview: interfaces, Wi-Fi, routes, ports.
.TP
.B wellpower, power, wpower, wbatt
Battery wear, cycles, charge thresholds, power profiles.
.TP
.B welldoctor, doctor, wdoc, wdoctor
Health aggregator for cron: S.M.A.R.T., temperatures, units, disk usage.
.TP
.B whtml, html, report
Offline, self-contained HTML system report.
.TP
.B self-update, selfupdate
Same as \fBwellup \-\-self-update\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|eng"
Persistently set the report language. \fBru\fR, \fBen\fR and \fBeng\fR are
accepted. The setting is stored in
.I ~/.config/wellutils/lang.conf
and honoured by all tools in the suite.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " LANG"
Same as \fB\-\-lang\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Forwarded to the sub-tool: machine-readable JSON on stdout. Works for
every tool in the suite.
.TP
.BR \-\-plain ", " \-\-box ", " \-\-color ", " \-\-short ", " \-\-html ", " \-\-no\-emoji
Common output flags, forwarded to the sub-tool (dropped for
\fBwhtml\fR, which only writes HTML).
.TP
.I other \-\-options
Any other option given before the command (e.g.
\fBwellutils \-\-all fetch\fR) is passed to the tool unchanged, after
the command; the tool decides whether it is valid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the persistent language file; defaults to
.I ~/.config
. When neither \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR nor \fBHOME\fR is set, \fB\-\-lang\fR
refuses to save (nothing is written to /tmp); use \fBWELLUTILS_LANG\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wellutils/lang.conf
Persistent language setting.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/lang.sh
Translation table shared by the suite.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wellutils/box.sh
Shared box-drawing engine.
